No other test binds port 8000.

== Criteria for the part done here, written before the change ==
D1  test.yml's backend job starts the backend before pytest, the way the README does (sourcing the committed env
    example, uvicorn on :8000), waits for /ready to answer 200 - the demo tests' own up-check - and fails the job,
    printing the server log, if it never does.
D2  Proven locally first, since only CI can prove the CI half: the same commands start a server that /ready answers,
    and with it up the four demo tests run and pass rather than skip.
D3  Guard: test.yml's backend job must start a backend before its pytest step, so the demo tests cannot silently go
    back to skipping in CI. Sabotage: delete the step, and move it after pytest; both must turn the guard red.
D4  After a push, if the owner approves one: the CI pytest run shows the four demo tests passed, not skipped.
